(defun fact (n)
  (if (<= n 1) 1
    (* n (fact (- n 1)))))

(defun range (n)
  (letrec ((go (lambda (i acc)
          (if (< i 1) acc (go (- i 1) (cons i acc))))))
    (go n nil)))
(defmacro unless (test &rest body) (list 'if test nil (cons 'progn body)))

(try
  (risky)
  (catch (e)
    (princ e)))

Prose sits between the forms, and it keeps its punctuation: a comma,
a semicolon; a `backtick`, an apostrophe's tail and a "quoted phrase".
(princ (fact 5))
Trailing thought.
